   1. What is the lojban word for "imperative"?
http://vlasisku.lojban.org/redirects a search for "imperative" to
{ko}.
   2. How would one say something like "Let's go." in lojban.  i.e. an
   imperative directed at a group of which the speaker is a part.  Would it
   just be {ko klama}?
   3. (only loosely related to imperatives, but it's in the same train of
   thought for me)  How does one say something like "Long live the king.",
   which I think of (with my non linguistically-trained mind) as an imperative
   directed at the universe, synonymous with "May the king live long."


-- 
          Alex R

